// Core standard library module: Io
// Provides file I/O operations and File handle methods.

// Static Io namespace:
// Io.open(path)                  - Opens a file handle of type Io.File.
// Io.read(path)                  - Reads the entire file content as string.
// Io.write(path, content)        - Writes string content to file (creates or overwrites).
// Io.copy(from, to)              - Copies a file to destination path.
// Io.move(from, to)              - Moves/renames a file to destination path.
// Io.delete(path)                - Deletes the file.
// Io.size(path)                  - Returns file size in bytes.
// Io.exists?(path)               - Checks if the file exists.
// Io.file?(path)                 - Checks if the path is a file.

// Io.File instance methods:
// file.content()                 - Reads the entire file content as string.
// file.write(text)               - Appends text to the file.
// file.reset()                   - Clears file content.
// file.delete()                  - Deletes the file.
// file.exists?()                 - Checks whether the file exists.
// file.empty?()                  - Checks whether the file is empty.
// file.size() / file.bytelen()   - Returns byte size of the file.
// file.linelen()                 - Returns line count.
// file.symlen()                  - Returns character count.
